ings 15; 16; 2 Chr. 16:1-6). He was the son of Ahijah of the tribe of Issachar.","verses":26,"father":"Ahijah","mother":"","v":[1,3,5,6]},{"id":"ben-hadad_452","name":"Ben-hadad","also":"","summary":"The king of Syria whom Asa, king of Judah, employed to invade Israel (1 Kings 15:18).","verses":18,"father":"Tabrimon","mother":"","v":[2,4]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[4]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[4]},{"id":"hanani_1379","name":"Hanani","also":"","summary":"A prophet who was sent to rebuke king Asa for entering into a league with Benhadad I., king of Syria, against Judah (2 Chr. 16:1-10).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[14]}],"places":[{"id":"ramah_972","name":"Ramah","kind":"City","lat":31.89964,"lon":35.20422,"summary":"A city first mentioned in Josh. 18:25, near Gibeah of Benjamin. It was fortified by Baasha, king of Israel (1 Kings 15:17-22; 2 Chr. 16:1-6).","verses":17,"v":[1,5,6]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[2]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[2,7]},{"id":"abel-maim_7","name":"Abel-maim","kind":"","lat":33.26853,"lon":35.57805,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[4]},{"id":"dan_323","name":"Dan","kind":"Region","lat":33.24856,"lon":35.65252,"summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":20,"v":[4]},{"id":"ijon_594","name":"Ijon","kind":"City","lat":33.32804,"lon":35.61188,"summary":"A ruin, a city of Naphtali, captured by Ben-hadad of Syria at the instance of Asa (1 Kings 15:20), and afterwards by Tiglath-pileser of Assyria (2 Kings 15:29) in the reign of Pekah; now el-Khiam.","verses":3,"v":[4]},{"id":"geba_447","name":"Geba","kind":"City","lat":31.85788,"lon":35.25976,"summary":"The hill, (2 Sam. 5:25 [1 Chr. 14:16, “Gibeon”]; 2 Kings 23:8; Neh. 11:31), a Levitical city of Benjamin (1 Kings 15:22; 1 Sam. 13:16; 14:5, wrongly “Gibeah” in the A.V.), on the north border of Judah near Gibeah (Isa. 10:29; Josh. 18:24, 28).","verses":14,"v":[6]},{"id":"mizpah_811","name":"Mizpah","kind":"City","lat":31.83274,"lon":35.18016,"summary":"A city of Benjamin, “the watch-tower”, where the people were accustomed to meet in great national emergencies (Josh. 18:26; Judg. 20:1, 3; 21:1, 5; 1 Sam. 7:5-16).","verses":30,"v":[6]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[7970,7970,7970,8141,609,609,609,1201,4428,3478,3478,5927,5927,5921,3063,1129,1129,7414,5414,5414,3318,3318,3318,935,935,935,935,609,609,4428,3063,3063],[609,609,3318,3701,3701,2091,2091,214,214,214,1004,1004,1004,3068,3068,3068,4428,4428,4428,1004,7971,7971,7971,7971,559,559,559,413,1130,4428,758,758,3427,3427,3427,1834,1834],[1285,1285,1285,1285,1285,996,996,996,996,996,996,996,996,1,1,1,1,1,2009,7971,7971,7971,0,3701,2091,2091,1980,1980,6565,6565,1285,1285,854,1201,4428,3478,3478,5927,5927,5927,5927,5